The hierarchical carbon-encapsulated yolk-shell nickelic composites were fabricated by a general MOF-derived route via Ostwald ripening and anion exchange strategy. Benefitting from the unique yolk-shell carbon framework, synergistic effect and satisfied phys-chemical characters, the nickel phosphide displays superior sodium storage properties compared with sulfide and selenide counterparts.
